# versions.env — NEMTUS image versions injected into shoestring.ini [images]
#
# Owned by the nemtus mirror layer. apply-nemtus-networks-patch.sh sources this file
# and rewrites the [images] client/rest entries of shoestring.ini (on every branch)
# to point at the NEMTUS ghcr.io images at THESE versions.
#
# IMPORTANT: only bump a version here AFTER the matching image has actually been
# published to ghcr.io/nemtus (see nemtus/symbol catapult-image-* / rest-image-* tags).
# Pinning a version that does not exist would make `docker compose pull` fail downstream.
#
# Tagging convention: pin the DATE-SUFFIXED IMMUTABLE tag, never the mutable
# `v<X>` one.
#
#   ghcr.io/nemtus/catapult-server:v1.0.3.9            <- mutable, moves on every rebuild
#   ghcr.io/nemtus/catapult-server:v1.0.3.9-20261101   <- immutable, one specific build
#
# Why: we rebuild these images at an UNCHANGED upstream version to pick up base-image
# security patches, which moves the mutable tag to a new digest. shoestring generates a
# docker-compose.yaml without `pull_policy`, and Compose defaults to `missing`, so a node
# that already has `v1.0.3.9` cached never re-pulls it — not on `docker compose up -d`,
# not after `shoestring upgrade`. A moved mutable tag therefore reaches NEW setups only
# and never reaches existing nodes. Changing the reference string here is what makes the
# rebuild visible to them, because shoestring re-downloads this repo's branch archive on
# every setup/upgrade and takes [images] from the shoestring.ini inside it.
#
# OPERATIONAL RULE: every time an image is rebuilt — including a same-version security
# rebuild — publish a new date-suffixed tag and bump it here, or existing nodes will
# keep running the old build forever.
#
# Upstream mapping (for reference):
#   symbolplatform/symbol-server:gcc-<X>  -> ghcr.io/nemtus/catapult-server:v<X>-<YYYYMMDD>
#   symbolplatform/symbol-rest:<Y>        -> ghcr.io/nemtus/symbol-rest:v<Y>-<YYYYMMDD>
#   mongo:<Z>                             -> kept as-is (third-party)
# where <YYYYMMDD> identifies the nemtus rebuild of that upstream version. Several dated
# tags can exist for one upstream version; the newest published one belongs here.
CATAPULT_IMAGE_VERSION=v1.0.3.10-20261114
REST_IMAGE_VERSION=v2.5.2-20261114
